# Loopback client
#
# Shows:   the client half of the loopback tour — `run` sending a paced burst,
#          each order chased and then cancelled, and `on sent order` minding
#          whatever you send by hand meanwhile
# Needs:   the loopback sessions with loopback-venue armed in Market Macros.
#          Run it on LOOP-CLI. Help > Macro Examples does all of it with
#          "Run the loopback tour"
# Watch:   Sent Orders and Received Trades; Client Macro Orders, one row an order
# Outcome: five orders go out at two a second; each is acknowledged, part
#          filled, replaced up once, and what is left is cancelled; every macro
#          passes. The run stays live, minding orders sent by hand on the same
#          session, until you stop it

macro loopback-client
seed 1
on error continue

# `run` names no session: Run… asks for one, so the same macro can be run on
# several sessions at once. `run on LOOP-CLI` would open Run… on that session.
run
    repeat 5 at 2/s with sym = ['IBM', 'MSFT']
        new symbol: sym, side: buy, qty: 100 * (n + 1), type: limit, price: 25.00
        expect ack within 2s else fail 'no acknowledgement'

        wait fill or timeout 3s
        if order.pending_action == '' and order.leaves_qty > 0
            replace qty: order.order_qty + 100
            wait replaced or cancel rejected or timeout 2s

        wait filled or timeout 2s
        if order.leaves_qty > 0
            cancel
            expect canceled or filled within 2s
        pass '${sym}: ${order.cum_qty} done'

# Anything sent by hand on the session this run was started on.
on sent order
    expect ack within 2s
    after 10s
    if order.leaves_qty > 0
        cancel
